 "content": "# Continual-ARC task insight\n\nSolved task `task-68aff4c6` (one demo, zero wrong submissions): combine two binary masks by pixelwise intersection/AND, output color 2 where both input masks are nonzero, otherwise 0. The demo represented masks side-by-side, separated by a vertical line of 7 (mask colors 1 and 9); output was the intersection. The test represented masks stacked vertically, separated by a full row of 3 (mask colors 4 and 5); output had 2 at cells occupied in both masks. Preserve the aligned mask dimensions; ignore separator and input colors. In the test, the lower mask covered every occupied cell of the upper mask, so the output equaled the upper mask's support.\n"
